    {
      "name": "spans_wide_enough_to_overrun_a_fixed_column",
      "why": "A cell's width is a function of measured data: `format_ratio_bounded` sizes its interval from the observed span, so no constant is provably sufficient. These values are chosen to exceed a fixed width rather than to depict a likely run -- and the margin matters, because the width of 22 that two tables carried was NOT overrun by an ordinary outlier. A 300ms repetition against a 4ns one renders 21 characters. Reaching 23 needs a hundredfold ratio as well. The argument for deriving the width is that the bound cannot be established, not that 22 was obviously too small.",
